# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
if flag.crooked_cause == "wipe"
Narrator: You fell together in the bloodied mire before the Born King, your weapons slipping from cold fingers as his great bellow shook the hills.
Narrator: With no hand left to stay him, the Horned King drives his antlers into the Crooked Tree and splits the ancient prison from crown to root.
endif
if flag.crooked_cause == "ritual_failed"
Narrator: Six times the demand was spoken over the goat skull, and six times the refusal echoed back through the hollow dark.
Narrator: Starved of sacrifice, the binding snaps in reverse, and the ritual finishes in the dark queen's favour with a roar of green flame.
endif
if flag.crooked_cause == "refused"
Narrator: When the last offering was called for, one among you held back, leaving Lord Phillip's desperate plea unanswered in the cold air.
Narrator: The unfinished circle breaks like dry kindling, and the ember dies before it ever touches the bark of the Crooked Tree.
endif
Narrator: Kehlenn rises unchecked toward the crone's face in the sky, her laughter rattling every windowpane across the valley of Druskenvald.
Narrator: Great black roots burst up through the cobblestones of the Founder's Round, tearing through the timber roofs and hearthstones of Wickermoor.
Narrator: Out in the tall grain of Foxwillow, the farming folk fold into dark feathers, rising as flocks of hoarse crows over the ruined fields.
the_vagrant [sad]: The old bough bent the whole way down tonight, and there is nothing straight left standing in the hollow.
Narrator: All the realm is unmade and born anew in her crooked image, beneath a moon that fills the whole dark heaven.
-> END
